# Cargo package: the sum is of Buildroot's vendored, re-packed archive
# (see bmcd.hash for the toolchain trap this shares).
#
# The version is commit a337773 on excavador-turing/tpi, released as v1.6.0:
# `firmware install` no longer decides whether a version exists -- the board
# does. The cached listing informs the confirmation line and cannot refuse.
# v1.5.0 and v1.5.1 both tried to make that listing fresh instead; the board
# answers 400 in 0.48 s for a version nobody has, so there was nothing to
# protect against. Also: `list --refresh` waited 60 s for polls that take
# 74-140 s and then printed the stale listing silently; four minutes now, and
# it says when it gives up.
#
# Measured 2026-09-10 with rust-bin 1.98.1 in the pinned container: `make
# tpi-source` reported got d7eaf605 against a zeroed expectation, then
# re-run to confirm it fetches and verifies cleanly.
sha256  d7eaf605ce1775a7269bbf8b95885071b73f965eebbd9ac1e3b6eebac2c81002  tpi-a337773ee4016332430e87e8bf53455e9c1dbe50-cargo2.tar.gz
